#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:54
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A 'triage: <date>' bean note on each theme's epic; new or re-parented beans; claims via beans:claim. Owning sessions still alive are notified before their branches are touched."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:37
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agents stalled, or owner asks to pick up their work"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Collect or reconstruct a handover report per agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Consolidate into 2-4 themes, with a recommendation each"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:50
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decide each theme"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Decides one theme at a time: continue, fold into the plan, new epic, park, or scrap."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:38
#. Diagram label
msgid "Find the footprint"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:58
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Green, up-to-date PRs join the queue; mid-merge branches are re-driven from the PR head, never guessed at; red PRs go back to the new driver."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Group by what the work delivers, not by agent. Each theme gets its epic, members, dependencies, risk, and one of: continue, fold in, new epic, park, scrap (owner only)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "handover notes (beans/notes, title 'handover:'), open PRs and branches by session or time window, in-progress beans, workflow instances, last PR and issue comments. REST, one batched pass."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:57
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-route open PRs that lost their driver"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:17
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads the footprint the stalled agents left, collects or reconstructs a handover report per agent, groups the work into 2-4 themes, and recommends. It never finishes, closes or deletes another agent's work."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Receives the open PRs that lost their driver: which are green and ready, which are mid-merge, which must be re-driven from their PR head."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:53
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the triage and claim the picked-up work"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled work has an owner and a place in the plan"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:11
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage: collect handovers, consolidate themes, recommend, re-route"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:16
#. Diagram label
msgid "Triage agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Use the agent's own report and check it against live state; if none, ask the agent if it is still reachable, else reconstruct with the handover-report template and mark it reconstructed. Unpushed state is unknown, never empty."
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:31
#. Diagram label
msgid "User"
msgstr ""

#: processes/sdlc/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn:14
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "When agents stall (context exhausted, container lost, session timed out) their work is spread over PRs, branches, beans and process runs. Collect each agent's handover report, or reconstruct one, group the work into 2-4 themes, recommend how to pick each up, let the user decide, then record it and re-route open PRs through the merge steward. Owner, 2026-10-02: 'an incoming stalled agent triage process which needs to look at stalled agents (named or over a given time window from active PRs, branches, discussions, beans etc), try to get as many handover reports as possible, if many then consolidate the various workstreams into 2-4 themes, give recommendation on how to pick up the work as part of current/new workplan; if open PRs etc, coordinate with relevant agents (e.g. the Merge Manager)'. Operating skills: stalled-agent-triage, handover-report."
msgstr ""
